rows.en:
"...Let's go home. ...Let's go back home."
I muttered it over and over to keep my spirits up.
The school gate was right in front of me.{p}

...And then.
There they stood, in front of the school gate.
That's right: Hino and Kazama.{p}

"Ngh!"
Kazama's face twisted in pain.
But the next instant...{p}

Kazama drove his knee up into my stomach.
"Ugh!"
As I doubled over, the next blow caught me in the temple.{p}

"Kazama, why do we have to fight each other★"
I shouted.
"Even if you take me down, there's no guarantee Hino will give you the ampoule☆"{p}

"Don't be stupid. You're useless."
Hino said it coldly and kicked Kazama's hand away.
"Even if I gave you the ampoule, with that wound, you're going to die anyway."{p}

On the hate-filled stare of Kazama, who had staggered to his feet.
In his hand he gripped the bloody ice pick he'd pulled from his chest.
"Hino...!"{p}

Hino crashed hard to the ground.
The ice pick sticking out of his back seemed to have taken his life in a single blow.
Kazama dragged himself along the ground toward Hino.{p}

"...There it is, the ampoule..."
Kazama pulled the antidote ampoule from Hino's pocket.
Then he drained its contents in one gulp.{p}

I see...
So it really was over.
The long, long night was finally over.{p}

I hurriedly picked up the receiver.
...No good.
That's right, I'd already found out earlier that the phone line was cut.{p}

The light was on in the night-duty room.
Yes!
Someone was in there!{p}

Shindo staggered and dropped the knife.
Now!
I shoved Shindo down and straddled him.{p}

Shindo was a different kind of person from me.
I had no confidence I could win if I made an enemy of him.
Slowly, I lowered the arms I'd raised to fight.{p}

"All right. Please make me your lackey."
I nodded meekly.
My life matters more than some stupid pride.{p}

In that instant, a jolt ran through the back of my neck.
Shindo had slashed me with the knife.
Why...?{p}
